I think the game is over.

277
00:10:40,975 --> 00:10:42,975
And that ends Hoopla!

278
00:10:42,975 --> 00:10:44,975
Thank you for coming!

279
00:10:44,975 --> 00:10:46,975
- Yeah! - Yeah!

280
00:10:46,975 --> 00:10:48,975
- Yeah! - Yeah!

281
00:10:48,959 --> 00:10:50,959
That was great, Mouse.

282
00:10:50,959 --> 00:10:51,959
Who won?

283
00:10:51,959 --> 00:10:52,959
Who knows?

284
00:10:52,959 --> 00:10:53,959
We don't keep score.

285
00:10:53,959 --> 00:10:54,959
It's just fun to play.

286
00:10:54,959 --> 00:10:57,959
Mr. Mouse, can I have your arm?

287
00:10:57,959 --> 00:10:58,939
I'm going to play.

288
00:10:58,943 --> 00:10:59,783
- Of course.

289
00:10:59,783 --> 00:11:03,783
Hmm, since we don't have any paper,

290
00:11:03,783 --> 00:11:07,783
I'll autograph my hoopla stick and let you keep it.

291
00:11:07,783 --> 00:11:08,923
- Whoa!

292
00:11:08,927 --> 00:11:11,727
- Oh, thanks, woo-pee!

293
00:11:11,727 --> 00:11:13,127
- That was nice, Mouse.

294
00:11:13,127 --> 00:11:16,667
- But if I'm going to keep playing hoopla, then?

295
00:11:16,667 --> 00:11:18,907
- You'll need a new stick.

296
00:11:18,911 --> 00:11:21,911
Here you go. Now you can play more hoopla.

297
00:11:22,491 --> 00:11:25,251
This doesn't feel quite like a hoopla stick, Oliver.

298
00:11:25,331 --> 00:11:28,891
This is another kind of stick entirely.

299
00:11:28,895 --> 00:11:33,895
If you give a mouse a stick, what do you think will happen next?

300
00:11:38,879 --> 00:11:40,379
Over there, Oliver.

301
00:11:40,379 --> 00:11:41,719
You missed a red one.

302
00:11:41,719 --> 00:11:42,719
Got it.

303
00:11:42,719 --> 00:11:43,959
Thanks, Mouse.

304
00:11:43,959 --> 00:11:44,959
Oh!

305
00:11:44,959 --> 00:11:45,959
That's a good one.

306
00:11:45,959 --> 00:11:46,959
Oh!

307
00:11:46,959 --> 00:11:48,859
That's a good one.

308
00:11:48,863 --> 00:11:50,203
And a yellow one.

309
00:11:50,203 --> 00:11:52,943
And a blue speckled one with neon writing.

310
00:11:52,943 --> 00:11:54,663
Blue speckled one?

311
00:11:55,663 --> 00:11:57,443
That's a candy wrapper.

312
00:11:57,443 --> 00:11:58,843
Oh, from a candy wrapper?

313
00:11:58,847 --> 00:12:01,147
- Candy wrapper tree? - Probably not.

314
00:12:01,147 --> 00:12:02,967
Oh, I've got a stick stuck.

315
00:12:02,967 --> 00:12:04,807
- Or a stuck stick.

316
00:12:04,807 --> 00:12:07,007
- Or a sticky stick stuck.

317
00:12:07,007 --> 00:12:08,827
- Sticky, sticky, sticky.

318
00:12:08,831 --> 00:12:11,331
Wait! Can I have that?

319
00:12:11,331 --> 00:12:14,171
The stick? Sure. What for?

320
00:12:14,171 --> 00:12:15,831
What for?

321
00:12:15,831 --> 00:12:18,811
Oliver, this is the best stick!

322
00:12:18,815 --> 00:12:21,815
I've never seen a stickier stick.

323
00:12:21,815 --> 00:12:24,815
If you give him a stick, then...

324
00:12:24,815 --> 00:12:26,815
What?

325
00:12:26,815 --> 00:12:28,795
You'll use it as a bag.

326
00:12:28,799 --> 00:12:30,799
in a high wire act.

327
00:12:30,799 --> 00:12:32,799
Careful, Mouse!

328
00:12:34,799 --> 00:12:38,799
- - Oh! Whoa!

329
00:12:38,783 --> 00:12:40,783
Made it! Ta-da!

330
00:12:42,783 --> 00:12:44,783
And now, ladies and gentlemen,

331
00:12:44,783 --> 00:12:48,763
getting ready to pole vault over the croquet wire loop thingy is...

332
00:12:48,767 --> 00:12:51,307
Mouse! Mouse is going for the world record.

333
00:12:51,387 --> 00:12:52,527
Woohoo!

334
00:12:52,607 --> 00:12:54,027
He's getting quite the running start.

335
00:12:54,107 --> 00:12:56,727
He'll need that speed to vault himself really high. Over!

336
00:12:57,607 --> 00:12:58,747
Woohoo!

337
00:12:58,751 --> 00:13:00,751
Mouse, you okay?

338
00:13:00,751 --> 00:13:03,751
It's a new world record!

339
00:13:03,751 --> 00:13:05,751
For mice, anyway.

340
00:13:05,751 --> 00:13:06,751
Oh, whoops!

341
00:13:06,751 --> 00:13:08,731
Gotcha!

342
00:13:08,735 --> 00:13:10,035
And this one too.

343
00:13:11,275 --> 00:13:12,275
That's all of them.

344
00:13:12,275 --> 00:13:14,535
Uh-oh. Come back here, Leaf.

345
00:13:17,235 --> 00:13:18,715
You can't get away from me.

346
00:13:18,719 --> 00:13:22,099
Hey, those sounds are kind of like music.

347
00:13:22,859 --> 00:13:24,459
Yeah, they are.

348
00:13:28,703 --> 00:13:38,683
If a mouse makes musical sounds with a stick, then...

349
00:13:38,687 --> 00:13:48,667
He'll want to find more sounds he can make with a stick.

350
00:13:48,671 --> 00:13:51,051
Hi, dog.

351
00:13:51,211 --> 00:13:51,751
Hi, mouse.

352
00:13:53,191 --> 00:13:54,991
Ooh, catchy tapping.

353
00:13:58,655 --> 00:14:08,635
- Oh, listen to that.

354
00:14:08,639 --> 00:14:09,479
- What's that?

355
00:14:12,639 --> 00:14:13,639
Hi, guys.

356
00:14:16,139 --> 00:14:18,619
- Hey, I have an idea.

357
00:14:18,623 --> 00:14:22,463
We all play music at the same time, then...

358
00:14:22,463 --> 00:14:25,463
We can be an animal band!

359
00:14:25,463 --> 00:14:26,463
We're a band.

360
00:14:26,463 --> 00:14:28,603
Oh, I mean a band!

361
00:14:28,607 --> 00:14:31,487
Hey, you guys, I'm in a band.

362
00:14:31,527 --> 00:14:32,527
Isn't that amazing?

363
00:14:38,591 --> 00:14:40,631
Animal band coming through!

364
00:14:40,631 --> 00:14:43,631
If I see an animal band then...

365
00:14:45,631 --> 00:14:48,571
Ha-ha-ha-ha!

366
00:14:48,575 --> 00:14:51,575
I just have to join in.

367
00:14:56,575 --> 00:14:58,555
Oh, can I be playing?

368
00:14:58,559 --> 00:15:00,439
- Are you part of the animal band too?

369
00:15:00,439 --> 00:15:01,439
- Of course.

370
00:15:01,439 --> 00:15:02,439
- Follow us, Moose.

371
00:15:06,479 --> 00:15:08,539
- Wow, if a mouse goes away

372
00:15:08,543 --> 00:15:13,543
tapping a stick, then he may come back

373
00:15:14,223 --> 00:15:18,523
with a whole animal band.

374
00:15:18,527 --> 00:15:28,507
- Whoa!

375
00:15:28,511 --> 00:15:30,851
- Oh, we sung!

376
00:15:30,851 --> 00:15:33,091
- An animal band, love it.

377
00:15:33,091 --> 00:15:34,771
I've gotta go finish raking,

378
00:15:34,771 --> 00:15:37,711
but I can't wait to hear what you do next.

379
00:15:37,711 --> 00:15:38,491
- Huh.

380
00:15:38,495 --> 00:15:40,495
What are we gonna do next?

381
00:15:41,155 --> 00:15:43,155
I know. Write a song!

382
00:15:43,155 --> 00:15:45,155
That's a great idea!

383
00:15:45,155 --> 00:15:46,535
What should it be about?

384
00:15:46,535 --> 00:15:48,475
I think we should write a song about me.

385
00:15:48,479 --> 00:15:50,479
- I think we should write a song about a bone.

386
00:15:50,479 --> 00:15:51,479
- I think we should write a song about a horn.

387
00:15:51,479 --> 00:15:53,479
- Ooh, I think we should write a song about cows

388
00:15:53,479 --> 00:15:55,479
dancing in beautiful meadows

389
00:15:55,479 --> 00:15:58,459
in the springtime sniffing chrysanthemums.

390
00:15:58,463 --> 00:16:05,463
Well, that's what I think we should write a song about.

391
00:16:05,463 --> 00:16:08,443
That's it!

392
00:16:08,447 --> 00:16:11,527
- I think we should write a song about.

393
00:16:11,527 --> 00:16:12,567
- About what?

394
00:16:12,567 --> 00:16:13,647
You stopped singing.

395
00:16:13,647 --> 00:16:14,987
- That's where you join in.

396
00:16:14,987 --> 00:16:17,067
See, I was inspired to write a song

397
00:16:17,067 --> 00:16:18,427
where we say what we think

398
00:16:18,431 --> 00:16:20,431
what this song should be about.

399
00:16:20,431 --> 00:16:23,271
So if I think it should be a song about a stick,

400
00:16:23,271 --> 00:16:28,411
I could go...

401
00:16:28,415 --> 00:16:30,375
We should write a song about a stick.

402
00:16:30,375 --> 00:16:34,255
I'd come up with lots of words for it quick.

403
00:16:34,255 --> 00:16:36,455
That's our song, sing along.

404
00:16:36,455 --> 00:16:38,395
Let's all sing about singing a song.

405
00:16:38,399 --> 00:16:41,399
Ooh, I think we should write a song about--

406
00:16:41,399 --> 00:16:44,399
Trees, it's much more pleasant than singing about your knees.

407
00:16:45,399 --> 00:16:48,379
That's our song, sing along.

408
00:16:48,383 --> 00:16:52,223
Let's all sing about singing a song.

409
00:16:52,223 --> 00:16:53,923
I think we should write a song about--

410
00:16:53,923 --> 00:16:56,223
Oh, that lovely shed behind your house.

411
00:16:56,223 --> 00:16:58,363
But I can't think of what rhymes with

412
00:16:58,367 --> 00:17:00,327
with shed behind your house.

413
00:17:00,327 --> 00:17:01,707
Ooh, Mouse?

414
00:17:01,707 --> 00:17:03,707
That's our song, sing along.

415
00:17:03,707 --> 00:17:07,467
Let's all sing about singing our song.

416
00:17:07,467 --> 00:17:08,347
I think we should write

417
00:17:08,351 --> 00:17:09,191
- A bone!

418
00:17:09,191 --> 00:17:11,191
- A bone is really delicious and crunchy

419
00:17:11,191 --> 00:17:14,191
and delicious and awesome and I like them!

420
00:17:14,191 --> 00:17:16,191
- That's our song, sing along!

421
00:17:16,191 --> 00:17:18,331
Let's all sing about singing along!

422
00:17:18,335 --> 00:17:20,335
in our song.

423
00:17:20,335 --> 00:17:22,335
I think we should write a song about--

424
00:17:22,335 --> 00:17:23,335
Milk.

425
00:17:23,335 --> 00:17:25,335
Scuba-dooba-scabba-dabba-rappa-snappa-snappa.

426
00:17:25,335 --> 00:17:26,335
No.

427
00:17:26,335 --> 00:17:28,315
Scuba-dooba-scabba-dabba-rappa-snappa.

428
00:17:28,319 --> 00:17:32,819
Scuba-duba-scabba-dabba-rappa-rappa-snappa-snappa-spilk?

429
00:17:32,919 --> 00:17:33,819
Nah.

430
00:17:33,919 --> 00:17:36,819
Scuba-duba-scabba-dabba-rappa-rappa-snappa-sapa-silk!

431
00:17:36,919 --> 00:17:38,299
That's it!

432
00:17:38,303 --> 00:17:41,243
That's our song, sing along.

433
00:17:41,243 --> 00:17:43,803
Let's all sing about singing a song.

434
00:17:43,803 --> 00:17:44,803
One more time.

435
00:17:44,803 --> 00:17:47,303
That's our song, sing along.

436
00:17:47,303 --> 00:17:48,283
Let's all sing about singing a song.

437
00:17:48,287 --> 00:17:51,287
about singing a song.

438
00:17:51,287 --> 00:17:53,287
I wish we could play for an audience

439
00:17:53,287 --> 00:17:55,287
so someone could clap for us.

440
00:17:55,287 --> 00:17:57,287
I know where there's an audience.

441
00:17:57,287 --> 00:17:58,267
Esme Louise is having a fun.

442
00:17:58,271 --> 00:17:59,811
a tea party at our house.

443
00:17:59,811 --> 00:18:00,611
Brilliant!

444
00:18:00,611 --> 00:18:03,231
She'll need music for sure.

445
00:18:03,231 --> 00:18:04,231
Follow me, let's go!

446
00:18:04,231 --> 00:18:08,251
MUSIC

447
00:18:08,255 --> 00:18:10,255
Hi, Esme Louise!

448
00:18:10,255 --> 00:18:12,255
We hear you're having a tea party.

449
00:18:12,255 --> 00:18:14,255
That is true.

450
00:18:14,255 --> 00:18:17,255
I decided to have a party for my statue of Beethoven.

451
00:18:17,255 --> 00:18:18,235
My brother's a little girl.

452
00:18:18,239 --> 00:18:19,899
and my broken clock.

453
00:18:19,999 --> 00:18:23,039
If you're going to have a tea party, then...

454
00:18:25,219 --> 00:18:28,219
You're definitely going to need some music.

455
00:18:28,223 --> 00:18:30,063
A lovely idea.

456
00:18:30,063 --> 00:18:32,063
Do you know any music by Beethoven?

457
00:18:32,063 --> 00:18:33,063
It depends.

458
00:18:33,063 --> 00:18:36,223
Did Beethoven write anything for squeaky horn?

459
00:18:36,223 --> 00:18:38,203
Hmm.

460
00:18:38,207 --> 00:18:39,367
I don't think so.

461
00:18:39,367 --> 00:18:40,367
Wait a minute.

462
00:18:40,367 --> 00:18:42,047
I know a tea time song.

463
00:18:44,207 --> 00:18:44,907
Listen.

464
00:18:44,907 --> 00:18:46,847
Everybody gather round.

465
00:18:46,847 --> 00:18:48,187
Time for a tea time.

466
00:18:48,191 --> 00:18:49,031
Go down!

467
00:18:53,191 --> 00:18:54,831
Everybody gather round

468
00:18:54,831 --> 00:18:56,731
Now all of you hop up and down

469
00:18:56,731 --> 00:18:58,171
Hop up and down

470
00:18:58,175 --> 00:19:00,175
Up, up, and down

471
00:19:00,175 --> 00:19:02,255
Tea time, low down

472
00:19:02,255 --> 00:19:04,175
Up, up, and down

473
00:19:04,175 --> 00:19:08,175
Everybody gather

474
00:19:08,159 --> 00:19:10,159
Now all of you please dance around

475
00:19:10,159 --> 00:19:12,159
Dance around

476
00:19:12,159 --> 00:19:14,159
Dance around

477
00:19:14,159 --> 00:19:16,159
Tea time hold down

478
00:19:16,159 --> 00:19:18,139
Dance around

479
00:19:18,143 --> 00:19:28,123
Everybody gather round, now be quiet, not a sound, not a sound, not a sound.

480
00:19:28,127 --> 00:19:32,467
Tea time all down, not a sound.

481
00:19:32,467 --> 00:19:36,467
Everybody gather round.

482
00:19:36,467 --> 00:19:37,467
The tea is ready.

483
00:19:37,467 --> 00:19:38,107
It's time to go.

484
00:19:38,111 --> 00:19:41,111
But before we do, please dance some more.

485
00:19:44,111 --> 00:19:46,111
Dance some more, dance some more.

486
00:19:46,111 --> 00:19:48,091
Keep time, hold down, get it.

487
00:19:48,095 --> 00:19:50,935
Dance some more, dance some more.

488
00:19:50,935 --> 00:19:52,975
Dance some more.

489
00:19:52,975 --> 00:19:56,335
Tea Time Hotel, dance some more.

490
00:19:56,335 --> 00:19:58,075
Oh, yeah!

491
00:19:58,079 --> 00:19:59,579
That was excellent.

492
00:19:59,579 --> 00:20:03,619
Your tonalities blended to produce a very musical sound.

493
00:20:03,619 --> 00:20:04,959
Yay!

494
00:20:04,959 --> 00:20:06,079
What did she say?

495
00:20:06,079 --> 00:20:07,179
It was good.

496
00:20:07,179 --> 00:20:08,059
Yay!

497
00:20:08,063 --> 00:20:09,723
It was good!

498
00:20:09,823 --> 00:20:11,403
Oh, look at the hour!

499
00:20:11,503 --> 00:20:14,063
I need to take a bath and comb my hair before dinner.

500
00:20:14,163 --> 00:20:16,563
Alas, I will need my comb back.

501
00:20:16,663 --> 00:20:18,043
No problem.

502
00:20:18,047 --> 00:20:19,207
Dinner.

503
00:20:19,307 --> 00:20:21,847
Oh, I have a souffle that needs to go in the oven

504
00:20:21,947 --> 00:20:23,327
before dinner time.

505
00:20:23,427 --> 00:20:24,187
Dinner time?

506
00:20:24,287 --> 00:20:25,187
Oh, gotta go.

507
00:20:25,287 --> 00:20:26,427
I should go, too.

508
00:20:26,527 --> 00:20:27,487
Bye, Mouse.

509
00:20:27,587 --> 00:20:28,027
Bye.

510
00:20:28,031 --> 00:20:29,031
Bye, Mouse.

511
00:20:29,031 --> 00:20:30,031
Bye, everyone.

512
00:20:30,031 --> 00:20:32,031
Great playing today.

513
00:20:32,031 --> 00:20:34,031
Hi, Oliver.

514
00:20:34,031 --> 00:20:35,031
Hi, Mouse.

515
00:20:35,031 --> 00:20:37,031
Oh, now you have two sticks.

516
00:20:37,031 --> 00:20:38,011
I made my way to the end.

517
00:20:38,015 --> 00:20:41,015
I'd break my one stick into two by breaking it in half.

518
00:20:41,015 --> 00:20:43,015
But now I'm done with both sticks

519
00:20:43,015 --> 00:20:45,015
because everyone in the band had to go home.

520
00:20:45,015 --> 00:20:47,995
If it's yard trimmings, then we put them in the green box.

521
00:20:47,999 --> 00:20:49,999
I like sorting things.

522
00:20:49,999 --> 00:20:51,999
Bye-bye stick.

523
00:20:51,999 --> 00:20:53,999
And other stick.

524
00:20:53,999 --> 00:20:55,999
Ready for dinner?

525
00:20:55,999 --> 00:20:57,979
Yep. If you spend a long time

526
00:20:57,983 --> 00:21:01,283
playing music, then you get hungry.

527
00:21:03,983 --> 00:21:05,483
Ooh, that was good.

528
00:21:05,583 --> 00:21:07,963
I love it when Mom makes mac and cheese.

529
00:21:07,967 --> 00:21:09,967
Me too.

530
00:21:10,967 --> 00:21:13,967
Oh, hey, Mouse. Just playing my squeak toy.

531
00:21:13,967 --> 00:21:17,947
That was so much fun being in a band.

532
00:21:17,951 --> 00:21:18,991
Oh, hi, Mouse.

533
00:21:19,111 --> 00:21:19,951
Hi, Dog.

534
00:21:20,091 --> 00:21:20,951
Hi, Pig.

535
00:21:21,051 --> 00:21:24,731
I was just remembering how much fun it was being in a band.

536
00:21:26,831 --> 00:21:27,931
Esme, Louise, please.

537
00:21:27,935 --> 00:21:30,095
I finished combing her hair.

538
00:21:30,095 --> 00:21:32,735
She had some tangles.

539
00:21:32,735 --> 00:21:34,735
- Hello, everyone. - Hi, Moose.

540
00:21:34,735 --> 00:21:37,915
Hey, our whole band is here.

541
00:21:37,919 --> 00:21:39,919
Are you thinking what I'm thinking?

542
00:21:39,919 --> 00:21:41,919
Our band! We could play again!

543
00:21:41,919 --> 00:21:44,919
Let's play! We have instruments.

544
00:21:44,919 --> 00:21:46,919
And we have a... uh-oh.

545
00:21:46,919 --> 00:21:47,899
We have an uh-oh?

546
00:21:47,903 --> 00:21:49,443
- Oh, what's an uh-oh?

547
00:21:49,443 --> 00:21:51,903
- I just realized what we don't have.

548
00:21:51,903 --> 00:21:53,203
An audience!

549
00:21:53,203 --> 00:21:56,103
The tea party ended, so who will clap for us?

550
00:21:56,103 --> 00:21:57,883
- Well, if you need an audience,

